      "message": "I think this paragraph describes the upstream path rather than the code this patch replaces: fast GUP is already off for 4KB processes (`gup_fast_permitted()`, aosp/4312491), and aosp/4312497 takes the slice from `vma_slice_offset()`, not from the virtual address. If the patch stays, could the message name the mappings whose PTE slice differs from `vma_slice_offset()`?",
