      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:30:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like inferring the slice from the VMA is still exact here: since aosp/4366901, aosp/4368054 and aosp/4368056, every 4KB PTE maps the slice that `vma_slice_offset()` gives its address, and aosp/4312497 reads it under `mmap_lock`, so file VMAs with `vm_slice_off !\u003d 0` already get the right bytes.\n\nAs far as I can see, the only exception is the driver-selected slices of `vm_insert_page_slice()` from aosp/4367599 (the `{ 3, 1, 0, 2 }` fixture in aosp/4367986). Is there another case you hit? If not, and those insertions can follow `vma_slice_offset()`, would it be OK to drop this patch?",
      "isAi": true,
      "revId": "d7a0dbdf67ddd01da62f2b1953795ffaddfa5cf7",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1a60cd06_666b732c",
