      "writtenOn": "2026-10-28T03:30:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If the PTE slice is needed, I\u0027m worried about limiting each extraction to one 4KB page. `p3s_get_user_slice_pages()` returns whole runs of consecutive slices, so a 1MB O_DIRECT read from an anonymous buffer can be a single extraction today, but takes 256 here, each with `mmap_read_lock()` and a page table walk.\n\nWould it work to keep `p3s_iov_iter_extract_pages()` and only change the slice source in `p3s_slice_run_merge()`, e.g. `spans[i].offset \u003e\u003e PAGE_SHIFT_4KB` from the range GUP instead of `vma_slice_offset()`? That keeps the runs, avoids a new function in `lib/iov_iter.c` and an unused `p3s_iov_iter_extract_pages()`, and also covers `process_vm_readv()`/`process_vm_writev()` (aosp/4312492), which use the same helper and which the aosp/4367986 fixture checks too.\n\nThis path also hits the userfaultfd `-EFAULT` from the missing `FOLL_UNLOCKABLE` that I mentioned on aosp/4367611.",
      "isAi": true,
